ople in  48 states who were prevented from  casting a ballot last year in the wider  political context it's also about the  struggle between those who want to  reduce voting rights and those who want  to increase them it's not just about  Congress it's about who controls the  courts the police stations and the  school boards the U.S has over half a  million elected officials and the demand  In This Crowd on this day is that they  represent all the country's people not  just some of them  Mike Hannah Al Jazeera Washington
 

